 "provenance": "Bavaria 6 (w1 l5) normal exit 36,6, control-only on the exact S700 core. Start: lives 12 (campaign-style value used by earlier routes), weaponTier 2 (hook obtained in Bavaria 3), maxHealth 4, 0 diamonds. Route: first 785 ticks replay the intent of the old port attempt bavaria-06-two-silver-gates (falling mine clears the first rubble, both silver-key chests, both silver locks, checkpoint 31,14). Then: hammer bridge switch 27,16 (bridges 25,16-17 open into the upper cavern); cut grass 24,15/24,14 and push mine 23,14 left along the grass until it drops onto grass 20,16, push it along row 15 over the closed bridges after toggling them with switch 16,15, toggle again so it drops onto bridge 17,17, push it left off 16,16 so it falls in column 15 and explodes on rubble 15,19 (clears 14-15,17-19); checkpoint 12,18, down the column-11 diamonds to checkpoint 13,25; switch 19,22 closes bridge 17,24, hook mine 15,23 from 18,23 (lands on 17,23), hook it again from 20,23 so it falls in column 19 and explodes on rubble row 27; switch 19,22 again closes bridge 21,24, hook mine 23,23 from 20,23 (lands on 21,23), hook it from 18,23 so it falls in column 19 and explodes on rubble row 28; open gold-key chest 19,29; return east over diamonds/grass, cut grass 30,19 and hammer grass 31,19 so stone 31,18 drops away, climb past checkpoint 31,14 and the snakes to 33,5 (gold lock 34,5 opens gate 34,6) and walk out through 36,6. Three snake bites in total (health 4 -> 1): the row-10 snake near 31-32,10 during the replayed part (t~753), the red snake at 23-25,25 on the way back east (t~1836) and the row-11 red snake below 31,10 on the climb (t~2002); no deaths, no resets.",
